Rule 7 (If ranks match, require exact shape match to ensure safe broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then shape(v_1) = shape(v_2)
>>
Rule 9 (tensors are broadcast-compatible, allowing scalar expansion)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 10 (tensors have exactly the same shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
